<title>USA: Manager invests in European tech stocks - Barron's.</title>
<headline>Manager invests in European tech stocks - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ralph Wanger, mutual fund manager of the Acorn Fund, said he was focusing on the European computer services industry, according to an article in Barron's business weekly.</p>
<p>He said the industry is strong worldwide and Europe has two particular demands -- the need to change computers for the the year 2000 and to adapt to the new unified currency.</p>
<p>The fund has holdings in Swedish WM-Data, Finland's TT Tieto Oy, and Getronics in the Netherlands, Barron's said.  </p>
<p>Wanger said he also was fond of various energy stocks, including CalEnergy Co Inc, AES Corp, and Seagull Energy.</p>
<p>Finally, Wanger told Barron's he considered the leisure industry a profitable business. His fund has holdings in Carnival Corp, Airtours Plc, and Genting International.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
